# Example .env for local development (loaded by `pnpm serve`).
# Copy to .env and adjust. NOTHING here is required: cour's only data
# source is AniList's public API, which needs no account or key. Every
# entry below is optional and shown with its default. Env vars override
# config.yaml (see config.example.yaml for the YAML equivalents).

# --- Optional: TMDB screenshot enrichment ---
# Adds screenshots to each title's details drawer. A TMDB v3 API key or
# v4 read token both work; everything else runs without it.
# TMDB_API_KEY=your-key-here

# --- Optional: season / deck tuning ---
# The served season auto-rotates one month ahead of the broadcast
# calendar (Dec 1 / Mar 1 / Jun 1 / Sep 1). Pinning EITHER value below
# disables that rotation -- pins are for testing, not normal operation.
# ANIME_SEASON=SUMMER         # WINTER | SPRING | SUMMER | FALL
# ANIME_YEAR=2026
# ANIME_SHOW_SEQUELS=false    # sequels hidden from the deck by default
# ANIME_CACHE_DIR=data/anilist

# --- Optional: HTTP server ---
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PORT=8000
# LOG_LEVEL=INFO              # DEBUG | INFO | WARNING | ERROR | CRITICAL
# ROOT_PATH=/cour             # sub-path prefix when behind a reverse proxy

# --- Optional: HTTP Basic Auth (set both to enable) ---
# Strongly recommended when cour is reachable beyond your LAN: rooms are
# gated only by knowledge of the room name.
# AUTH_USER=admin
# AUTH_PASS=changeme

# --- Optional: TLS (set both to serve https) ---
# TLS_CERT=/path/to/cert.pem
# TLS_KEY=/path/to/key.pem

# --- Optional: WebSocket Origin allowlist ---
# Comma-separated extra origins to accept beyond same-origin; needed when
# a reverse proxy serves cour under an origin that differs from its Host
# (see docs/reverse-proxy.markdown).
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://cour.example.com

# --- Optional: alternate config.yaml location ---
# CONFIG_PATH=/path/to/config.yaml
